<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- FABRICATED fixture. Reproduces the exact shape that made the Zennio Z40 and
     Z70 v2 panels REFUSE at pre-flight in the sweep: an enum parameter
     (<TypeRestriction>) whose declared default Value is NOT one of the
     enumeration's declared members. `compute_parameter_image` rejects it with
     "value `N` is not a declared enumeration member", which surfaces from
     plan_flash as `PlanError::UnresolvableImage: computing the parameter image`.

     Real cause observed (shape only, no vendor content copied):
       Z40  M-0071_A-51D1: param `...iconColor[0]`     default 3, enum has 0..2
       Z70  M-0071_A-5531: param `...pageDistribution[1]` default 0, enum lacks 0

     This is a genuine data-quality trap: the vendor's OWN default sits outside
     its OWN enum, and bussard's strict membership check refuses the whole
     download. Here the enum declares members {1,2} and the default is 3.

     Intended tests (bussard-prod + bussard-download):
       * `compute_parameter_image` returns an Err naming this parameter and the
         non-member value (pin the message shape).
       * `plan_flash` (mask 07B0) returns `PlanError::UnresolvableImage` whose
         reason contains "not a declared enumeration member".
       * A DECISION test for whether strict membership should hard-refuse a
         flashable device or fall back to encoding the raw number with a warning
         (see the sweep report: this refused 2 otherwise-executable panels). -->
